{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been feeling unwell. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been really tired, thirsty, and peeing a lot. My blood sugar has been over 500 even though I’ve been taking my insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any nausea, vomiting, or abdominal pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had vomiting at first, then diarrhea. My stomach hurts, and I haven’t been eating much. Also, my G-tube site has been draining something smelly and tender."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. We’ll check that. Your labs show very high blood sugar—697—and an elevated anion gap, which means you’re in diabetic ketoacidosis. We’re starting an insulin drip and fluids to correct that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’ve been taking my insulin. Why is this happening?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes illness or infection can make your body resist insulin. We’re also checking for infection at your tube site. An ultrasound showed no abscess, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had fevers too, low-grade. And I stopped smoking last week because I felt worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s smart. We’ll monitor your temperature. Right now, your priority is stabilizing your sugars and hydration. We’ll keep you in the ICU for close monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have pain medicine? My stomach really hurts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we can give you Dilaudid for pain. But we need to be careful with dosing because of your history of chronic pain and medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just need relief. I can’t sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2158-09-14 02:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll help with that. We’re also giving you Benadryl and Valium for anxiety and nausea. You’re in good hands."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2158-09-15 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your anion gap has closed, and your blood sugar is down to 206. That’s a big improvement. We’re transitioning you off the insulin drip to subcutaneous insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2158-09-15 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. But I noticed my GJ tube isn’t connected anymore. What happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2158-09-15 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "When you were transferred from ICU to the floor, the external part of the tube was missing. We don’t know how it came off. The site looks clean, no infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2158-09-15 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t do it. I don’t remember anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2158-09-15 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We believe you. But we need to replace it so you can get meds and feeds if needed. We’ll do that with radiology guidance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2158-09-15 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Do I need it? I’m eating a little now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2158-09-15 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right now, you’re tolerating small amounts, so we’re not starting feeds. But the tube is a safety net in case your gastroparesis flares again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2158-09-16 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to replace your GJ tube tomorrow. It’s a quick procedure under X-ray guidance. They’ll remove the old broken piece and put in a new one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2158-09-16 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2158-09-16 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Low risk. You’ll be sedated, and they’ll monitor you closely. The main risks are bleeding or infection, but we’ll watch for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2158-09-16 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m anxious about it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2158-09-16 09:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. We’ll give you extra diazepam beforehand to help you relax."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2158-09-17 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your Port-A-Cath isn’t working well for blood draws. A chest X-ray shows a possible disruption at the connection. We’ll inform your care team to avoid using it for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2158-09-17 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ll need more IVs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2158-09-17 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, yes. But we’ll work with radiology to see if it can be fixed or replaced later if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2158-09-18 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Ready for your procedure? They’ll retrieve the old tube fragment and place a new one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2158-09-18 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess. I just want this over with."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2158-09-18 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—the procedure went smoothly. They removed the broken tube and placed a new GJ tube. You’ll have it for safety, but you’re doing well with oral intake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2158-09-18 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2158-09-18 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Some soreness, but we’ll manage it with pain meds. Keep the site clean and dry. Let us know if it becomes red or drains."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugars are stable. We’re updating your insulin—70 units of long-acting at bedtime and Humalog with meals based on your sliding scale."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s more insulin than before. Why?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your body needed more during this illness. We’ll reassess at your follow-up. For now, consistency is key—eat regular meals and take insulin as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. But sometimes I just can’t eat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. That’s why the tube is there. But you’re doing better. Your labs are normal—no ketones, anion gap closed, electrolytes stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my pain meds? I need my Dilaudid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get 12 tablets to last until your pain clinic appointment. Please keep that appointment—it’s important for your pain contract."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I missed the last one. I was sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We called them and explained. They’re expecting you. Don’t miss it—your access to medication depends on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll go. I need help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’re discharging you today. You’re alert, walking, and stable. Any questions before we go over instructions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What do I do about the tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Flush it daily with water, even if not using it. Watch for redness, swelling, or drainage. If any, call your doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take 70 units of the long-acting at bedtime. Before meals and bedtime, check your sugar and use the sliding scale for Humalog. Eat consistent carbs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try to stay on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we ask. Follow up with your PCP and endocrinologist. Call if sugars are high, you feel sick, or the tube site looks infected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel better than I have in weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2158-09-18 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. Take care of yourself. You’re going home with a clear plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2158-09-18 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you understand your meds, the tube care, and when to call the doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2158-09-18 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. Insulin with meals, 70 at night, tube clean, call if sick or site looks bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2158-09-18 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll send your prescriptions to your pharmacy. Someone will walk you out soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2158-09-18 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2158-09-18 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2158-09-18 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—we updated your asthma meds. Keep using the fluticasone-salmeterol twice daily, and the albuterol as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2158-09-18 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been coughing a little, but it’s mostly old."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2158-09-18 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "As long as it’s not worsening, you’re fine. But use the inhalers as prescribed to keep it under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2158-09-18 16:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2158-09-18 16:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And take the omeprazole twice daily for now to protect your stomach, especially with ibuprofen use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2158-09-18 16:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll add that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2158-09-18 16:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve got it. We’ll see you in follow-up, but call sooner if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2158-09-18 16:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2158-09-18 16:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we can ask. Take it one day at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2158-09-18 16:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2158-09-14 02:08:00",
    "admission_end": "2158-09-18 19:17:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for diabetic ketoacidosis with hyperglycemia, abdominal pain, and purulent drainage from her GJ tube site. She was stabilized in the ICU with an insulin drip and IV fluids, resolving her DKA. During the hospitalization, the external portion of her GJ tube was found disconnected, and a fractured segment was retained in the stomach. She underwent a successful radiologically guided procedure to remove the fragment and replace the GJ tube. She improved clinically, tolerated oral intake, and was discharged home with updated insulin therapy, pain medication supply for her scheduled pain clinic visit, and instructions for tube site care. Her mental health and compliance were supported throughout by her medical guardian.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Hyposmolality and/or hyponatremia",
      "Mechanical complication of colostomy and enterostomy",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Disorders of magnesium metabolism",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Borderline personality disorder",
      "Attention to other artificial opening of digestive tract",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Tobacco use disorder"
    ]
  }
}
